# script-src hashes whitelist the page's remaining inline <script> snippets:
#   1) Organization JSON-LD (every page, sitewide in Base.astro)
#   2) Astro's IntersectionObserver loader (client:visible bootstrap)
#   3) Astro's astro-island custom-element registration
#   4) homepage JSON-LD @graph — WebSite + SoftwareApplication + FAQPage
#      (homepage only, in index.astro). The FAQ accordion is JS-free (native
#      <details>), so it adds no script hash.
#   5) /digital-waste-tracking JSON-LD @graph — Article + FAQPage +
#      BreadcrumbList (that page only). The DWTS timeline on it is driven by
#      an external module, so the page adds this one hash and no more.
#   6) /walkthrough JSON-LD @graph — BreadcrumbList only. Deliberately does NOT
#      include a VideoObject: the video isn't published yet, and a VideoObject
#      naming one that doesn't exist is a manual-action risk. Keeping the graph
#      static also means dropping the video in (two env vars) never touches this
#      hash. Adding VideoObject later DOES change it — regenerate then.
#   7) /install JSON-LD @graph — BreadcrumbList only.
# The player facade (src/scripts/walkthrough.ts) and the install-guide platform
# detector (src/scripts/install.ts) both import src/scripts/lib/env.ts, so they
# are emitted as external /_astro/*.js like the rest — neither adds a hash.
# The mobile-menu handler and the cinematic bundle are NO LONGER inline: they
# import a shared module (src/scripts/lib/env.ts), so Astro emits them as
# external /_astro/*.js files covered by script-src 'self'. Deliberate —
# inline-script hashes silently drift when the build minifier changes (this
# broke prod once, 13 Jul 2026); external 'self' scripts don't. Don't reinline.
# The 5 hashes below are stable (JSON-LD is plain JSON; Astro's runtime scripts
# don't re-minify per build). Regenerate only after an Astro version bump OR
# after editing:
#   - src/layouts/Base.astro (the Organization JSON-LD)
#   - src/pages/index.astro (the homepage JSON-LD @graph)
#   - src/pages/digital-waste-tracking.astro (its JSON-LD @graph) — note this
#     one is built from src/config/dwts.ts, so editing the FAQ or the
#     milestones in that config ALSO changes this hash.
#   - src/pages/walkthrough.astro or src/pages/install.astro (their @graphs)
#
# frame-src is the ONE third-party allowance on this site, and it exists for a
# single embed: the Cloudflare Stream player on /walkthrough. Three things keep
# it honest and all three must stay true —
#   1) It is CLICK-TO-LOAD. No iframe exists until the visitor presses play
#      (src/scripts/walkthrough.ts). That affirmative action is what makes the
#      embed lawful under PECR without a consent banner. Preloading, prefetching
#      or hover-triggering it would break that and make /cookies wrong.
#   2) frame-src ONLY. The player's own scripts run inside the iframe under
#      Cloudflare's policy, not ours, so no script-src/connect-src entry is
#      needed. The poster is a code-drawn SVG served from this origin, which is
#      why img-src stays 'self' data: — don't switch to a Stream thumbnail
#      without adding img-src and accepting the extra third-party request.
#   3) The wildcard covers the per-account `customer-<code>` subdomain, so
#      rotating the Stream account needs no header change. Any OTHER video host
#      is blocked outright — that is the intended behaviour, not a bug to work
#      around. Disclose in /cookies before you widen it.
# One-liner that prints the unique hashes across EVERY built page (globs
